[agent] **How it had to be done:** the external client's data paths were unreachable from this sandbox — direct connections to the cluster are blocked, the HTTP proxy covers only the REST API (the `NO_PROXY=10.0.0.0/8` env var had to be cleared so requests would even use it), ArrowFlight/Hopsworks Query Service reads hang (gRPC can't traverse the socks proxy), and Python-engine inserts fail because delta-rs writes straight to HopsFS on port 8020. So all real work ran **in-cluster**: I uploaded the CSVs plus a PySpark script via the dataset REST API and ran it as a Hopsworks job (`etl8af783`), which ingested both raw feature groups, did the platform-side join through the feature-store query API (`fg_a.select_all().join(fg_b.select_all())`), computed the rounded sum in Spark, and created/inserted the online-enabled derived feature group with `parents=[fg_a, fg_b]` for provenance. The job finished with `SUCCEEDED`, and a spot-check of the exported result (R00000: 10.0788 − 4.6348 = 5.444) matches.
